      {
        "id": 179306,
        "name": "Voob Gooblin",
        "username": "Voob_Gooblin",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/voob_gooblin/{size}/2504_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-07-26T17:02:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<blockquote><p><span>Triggers that say \"when a card is played\" and \"when a card enters play\" work the same way. They are normalized to \"when a card enters play\" in the video game.</span></p></blockquote><p>What about cards like Informant &amp; Trueshot?—do their effects now trigger both when a hero card is played and when a hero card is put into play by some other means? I always thought 'putting into play' was a way of getting around their effects—was that always incorrect? This concerns me.</p><p>Also, the Provocator Tarnis ruling: I wonder about similar \"the first time an x target does y etc.\" cards like Glamour, that seem to with function in the opposite way—is there a precedent setting here, or do we just have to take cards like this on a case by case basis? or is Tarnis an exception somehow?</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:03:39.549Z",
